# prompt id: providers.atria.json-output
# Source of truth for the Atria-only JSON-output hardening instructions.
#
# This BODY is sent to the LLM (it is genuine instruction text), so it lives
# under /prompts/providers/. The Atria EXECUTION/WIRING/VALIDATION stays in
# the provider adapter (src/server/integrations/ai/atria.ts): endpoint,
# secretRef, timeout, and the bounded response-normalizer policy.
#
# Compile rule (scripts/generate-ai-prompts.ts): lines that are blank or
# start with "#" are dropped; every remaining line is joined with a single
# space. Provider-neutral by construction: no model names, no auth syntax.
Return exactly ONE JSON object.
Return JSON only.
Do not return Markdown.
Do not wrap JSON in ``` fences.
Do not add explanations before or after JSON.
Do not return prose.
Do not return multiple JSON objects.
The JSON object must conform to the FlowPilot AI response contract.
Use only the allowed enum values.
Do not invent unknown fields.
The output must be directly parseable by JSON.parse().
